From 7a6c0f9a9edbe855502ba1293fb744a9d6f8e0d1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 02:42:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/6] krans: static context rANS coder (src/algo/krans.c), the
 kernel of graph leaf codec 33

Kolmo's own static rANS with static context modelling: 32-bit states in [2^16, 2^32), 12-bit
totals, 16-bit renormalisation words, 1-32 states over contiguous segments of a chunk (a byte's
context only looks back inside its segment, so the chains are independent). Context of a byte =
(bin of the summed magnitudes at up to four lags, bin of the previous byte with or without its
sign, phase); a run-coded context map sends the contexts onto at most 255 frequency tables, which
are coded as classes against the previous symbol with a few mantissa bits and one symbol taking
the rest of 2^12. The encoder merges contexts greedily on exact counts, reassigns them once to
the tables as built, and keeps the context set with the smallest exact score. The format is in
krans.h. tests/test_krans.c: round trips for every context set, truncated and corrupted payloads,
invalid headers, a tight output buffer and one pinned stream.

Review R02, claim ctx-rans-leaf (#11).

